Double-Ended Queue
======================
      allows insertion and removal of elements from both ends.
      Versatile, then regular queues and stacks because they support all the operations of both


     /* INSERTION METHODS */
     =======================

     addFirst(E e): Inserts the specified element at the front.
     addLast(E e):  Inserts the specified element at the end.
     offerFirst(E e):  Inserts the specified element at the front, if possible.
     offerLast(E e): Inserts the specified element at the end, if possible.


     /* REMOVAL METHODS */
     =======================

     removeFirst(E e): Retrieves and removes the first element.
     removeLast(E e):  Retrieves and removes the last element.
     pollFirst(E e):  Retrieves and removes the first element, OR returns null if empty.
     pollLast(E e):  Retrieves and removes the last element, OR returns null if empty.


    /* EXAMINATION  METHODS */
     =========================

     getFirst(E e): Retrieves, but does not remove the first element.
     getLast(E e):  Retrieves, but does not removes the last element.
     peekFirst(E e):  Retrieves, but does not remove the first element OR returns null if empty.
     peekLast(E e):  Retrieves, but does not removes the last element, OR returns null if empty.
